    <help><![CDATA[
**What it does**

AleRax is a parallel tool for species tree - gene tree inference and reconciliation
under gene duplication, loss, and horizontal gene transfer (HGT).

For each gene family, it takes as input a gene tree distribution (typically inferred
with Bayesian inference tools such as MrBayes or PhyloBayes).

**Two ways to use it**

- *You already have a species tree*: answer "Yes", select your tree, and keep the
  search on SKIP. AleRax reconstructs the history of each gene family
  on your tree.
- *You do not have a species tree*: choose "MiniNJ" and set the species tree search
  to HYBRID. AleRax first builds the species tree from the gene
  families, then reconstructs the history of each gene family on it.

**Inputs**

- A starting species tree: your own rooted tree (Newick), a MiniNJ estimate, or a random tree.
- A list collection of gene tree samples, one element per gene family.
- Optionally, a list collection of gene-to-species mapping files with the same element names.
  Each line of a mapping file contains a gene name and a species name, for example::

    ENSPTRP00000091955 PanUUUTroglodytes
    ENSCSAP00000007477 ChlorocebusUUUSabaeus

  Species names must be written exactly as in the species tree.

**Species tree search**

- SKIP: skip the species tree search (default)
- REROOT: only re-estimate the root of the starting species tree
- HYBRID: standard search (a mix of transfer-guided and local SPR moves)

**Reconciliation model**

- UndatedDTL (default): gene duplication, transfer and loss.
- UndatedDL: gene duplication and loss only (no transfers).
- Model parametrization: GLOBAL (default) estimates one set of rates for all families and
  species, PER-FAMILY one set per gene family, PER-SPECIES one set per species.
  According to the AleRax documentation, PER-SPECIES is not compatible with species tree
  inference, so use it only with SKIP.

**Advanced options**

- Number of samples: how many reconciled gene trees AleRax samples per family (default 100).
- Random seed: use the same seed to reproduce a run exactly (default 123).
- Archive: also return the complete AleRax results folder as one .tar file.

**Outputs**

- The species tree (your tree, or the one AleRax built).
- The AleRax log (settings used, progress and likelihood scores).
- The per-family likelihoods.
- A collection with the per-family event counts (duplications, transfers, losses per species).
- A collection with the per-family transfers (which species passed genes to which).
- Optionally, an archive with all result files.

**More information**

See the AleRax wiki: `Running AleRax <https://github.com/BenoitMorel/AleRax/wiki/Running-AleRax>`_,
`Gene-to-species mapping <https://github.com/BenoitMorel/AleRax/wiki/Gene-to-species-mapping>`_
and `Outputs <https://github.com/BenoitMorel/AleRax/wiki/Outputs>`_.
    ]]></help>
